From 0f2f42179a80d149468669f853aeabb4053b70bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:14:31 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(motion): the plan's crossing check excuses only a
 chord end at the other chord's END point

Review of #1134 (head d1dc959b): reading a chord end within TOUCH of the
other chord's LINE as a touch hid a walk passing through a chord at a
vertex a picometre off its interior (both of the walk's chords there
read as touching). The guard now uses the verifier's end-point-only
rule (#1129, CROSSING_TOUCH / proper_cross_touch): an end within 1 pm
of one of the other chord's end points reads as on its line; away from
end points the exact sign stays the law.

Pinned by a_walk_through_a_chord_at_a_vertex_a_picometre_off_its_line_still_crosses
(+-0.5 pm, at 0 / 37 / 1000 mm origins); a_contact_is_no_crossing_and_a_micron_past_is
now pins that a vertex a rounding past a chord's interior crosses.

Refs #1048

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
